{
	"quest.1667E289046B1A85.quest_desc": [
		"A Principle Vat on the yellow Athanor becomes a dropper. It lets the principles fall drop by drop, so no pipe needs to touch the Hollow."
	],
	"quest.1667E289046B1A85.title": "The Principle Dropper",
	"quest.177A062AE6D2B7A0.quest_desc": [
		"The fire that never goes out. Sal Ammoniac on the yellow Athanor gives it. A salamander will want it."
	],
	"quest.177A062AE6D2B7A0.title": "Ignis Perpetuus",
	"quest.1D9CF42169CEB2D1.quest_desc": [
		"Dragon's Breath on the red Athanor gives the screw for the Prelum, the press at the end of the Work."
	],
	"quest.1D9CF42169CEB2D1.title": "The Prelum Screw",
	"quest.1FF243EF7F4F8468.quest_desc": [
		"Raw copper on the white Athanor gives a seed of copper."
	],
	"quest.1FF243EF7F4F8468.title": "A Seed of Copper",
	"quest.234321D361F799B8.quest_desc": [
		"From my notebook, 2019:",
		"",
		"\"Red. The work ends in red. The Prelum presses the Caput Mortuum, the dead head, into netherite, and the Athanor burns like a sunset.",
		"",
		"The red fire burns. And now I want more.\"",
		"",
		"The last fire is Rubedo, the red one. Make either of the two seeds before this page, then tick it off.",
		"",
		"The journal's chapter Basel and Salzburg is your guide for this stage."
	],
	"quest.234321D361F799B8.quest_subtitle": "Journal: Basel and Salzburg",
	"quest.234321D361F799B8.title": "Rubedo: The Red Fire",
	"quest.29DD430DD256E06A.quest_desc": [
		"Ash is not yet Salt. The Purifier washes it out. It works with a Catch Basin and a Residue Crock for what the water leaves behind. The journal shows you how they stand."
	],
	"quest.29DD430DD256E06A.title": "Washing the Ash",
	"quest.2D27E165EDA376CC.quest_desc": [
		"An emerald on the red Athanor gives a seed of emerald."
	],
	"quest.2D27E165EDA376CC.title": "A Seed of Emerald",
	"quest.3BA0A2F507567BEF.quest_desc": [
		"The Prelum presses the Caput Mortuum, the worthless earth that stays when the Salt is gone, into netherite."
	],
	"quest.3BA0A2F507567BEF.title": "The Dead Head",
	"quest.3DD39C0BF6683C46.quest_desc": [
		"The Athanor is the heart of alchemy. It sits on a brick hearth and drinks the principles from three tanks around it. Alchemists call the whole road the Great Work: four fires, from black to red. Alone, the Athanor burns black. That is the first fire, Nigredo."
	],
	"quest.3DD39C0BF6683C46.title": "The Athanor",
	"quest.45C5249C3991B707.quest_desc": [
		"The yellow fire makes nobler seeds. Raw gold on the yellow Athanor gives a seed of gold."
	],
	"quest.45C5249C3991B707.title": "A Seed of Gold",
	"quest.4A8C8321E65C4EFD.quest_desc": [
		"Servus, kid,",
		"",
		"I owe you a confession. For forty years I was an alchemist. Not the kind that cheats kings out of their gold; the kind that reads.",
		"",
		"The family had a book: the journal of Paracelsus, the famous doctor and alchemist. The story goes that he stayed with the Hubers on his way to Salzburg and forgot it when he left. I never believed he forgot anything.",
		"",
		"My copy went down with the cellar. Make yourself a new one. The journal is your real guide down here; I only mark the milestones.",
		"",
		"Uncle Vinzenz"
	],
	"quest.4A8C8321E65C4EFD.quest_subtitle": "To be opened in your new cellar",
	"quest.4A8C8321E65C4EFD.title": "The Journal",
	"quest.51381E5AFF8B8E53.quest_desc": [
		"Liquid Salt runs through your fingers. The Coagulator sets it into crystals. It needs a Principle Vat; the journal shows how to build it."
	],
	"quest.51381E5AFF8B8E53.title": "Salt You Can Hold",
	"quest.60799F0F0C1365B5.quest_desc": [
		"From my notebook, 2003:",
		"",
		"\"The dose makes the poison. He wrote it, and I learned it the hard way, with a dropper and a burned sleeve. The yellow fire grows better seeds. And there is a fire spirit behind the burning gate.\"",
		"",
		"The third fire is Citrinitas, the yellow one. Make any one of the three things before this page, then tick it off.",
		"",
		"For the last fire, set Obsidian beside the tanks and offer the yellow Athanor a Ghast Tear. Red obelisks rise and the flame turns red.",
		"",
		"The journal's chapter on the wandering years is your guide for this stage."
	],
	"quest.60799F0F0C1365B5.quest_subtitle": "Journal: The Wandering Years",
	"quest.60799F0F0C1365B5.title": "Citrinitas: The Yellow Fire",
	"quest.69983347EA0BC160.quest_desc": [
		"A trading company trades. Take your first salt crystals to the warehouse and let a shuttle put them away. Salt again, like in 1521: the first goods of the new Huber \\& Co."
	],
	"quest.69983347EA0BC160.title": "Salt in the Racks",
	"quest.6A60D8F13A4F5802.quest_desc": [
		"Only the red fire makes the noblest seeds. A diamond on the red Athanor gives a seed of diamond."
	],
	"quest.6A60D8F13A4F5802.title": "A Seed of Diamond",
	"quest.70FBE2C8BA49454A.quest_desc": [
		"From my notebook, 1991:",
		"",
		"\"Forty years in the salt mine, and I never saw them. The elixir opened my eyes, and there they were: the little people in the rock. The gnomes grow the veins; we only dig them out.\"",
		"",
		"The second fire is Albedo, the white one. Make any one of the three things before this page, then tick it off.",
		"",
		"For the next fire, set an empty Principle Vat beside each tank and offer the white Athanor an Amethyst Block. Citrine grows in the vats and the flame turns yellow.",
		"",
		"The journal's chapter Schwaz is your guide for this stage."
	],
	"quest.70FBE2C8BA49454A.quest_subtitle": "Journal: Schwaz",
	"quest.70FBE2C8BA49454A.title": "Albedo: The White Fire",
	"quest.721EBED4B48FA286.quest_desc": [
		"The Receptaculum is a chest with a fire in its belly. What a homunculus gathers falls into it, and its fire keeps him warm.",
		"",
		"He needs a home first. Crying Obsidian on the red Athanor gives the Sealed Flask."
	],
	"quest.721EBED4B48FA286.title": "A Warm Chest",
	"quest.777FC09DFFCF8AA2.quest_desc": [
		"Quicksilver on the white Athanor gives the Elixir of Sight. Drink it and you see what lives in the rock."
	],
	"quest.777FC09DFFCF8AA2.title": "Elixir of Sight",
	"quest.7C2A969C37F1A51A.quest_desc": [
		"Raw ore will not take root. The seed of a metal does. Lay raw iron on the white Athanor."
	],
	"quest.7C2A969C37F1A51A.title": "A Seed of Iron",
	"quest.7C723D9D51CEADF2.quest_desc": [
		"From my notebook, 1984:",
		"",
		"\"Salt, Sulfur, Mercury. Everything comes apart into these three, if the fire is patient. I have the black fire now. Your great-grandmother would have called the priest.\"",
		"",
		"Lay a salt crystal on the Athanor and let the black fire grow it into a block. Sixteen of those blocks in a ring under the hearth turn the flame white.",
		"",
		"The journal's chapter Villach is your guide for this stage."
	],
	"quest.7C723D9D51CEADF2.quest_subtitle": "Journal: Villach",
	"quest.7C723D9D51CEADF2.title": "Nigredo: The Black Fire",
	"quest.7F5D364CF23DDAA8.quest_desc": [
		"The journal starts in Villach, with his father, metals and a fire. Build the Calciner the way it says: firebox at the bottom, then the ash pan, then the Calciner on top. It breaks almost anything down. What stays behind is ash."
	],
	"quest.7F5D364CF23DDAA8.title": "A Furnace That Breaks Things Down"
}
